{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_38","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"/home/agent-home/.codex/tmp/arg0/codex-arg0tkEFmF/apply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: /workspace/paper/paper.tex\n@@\n-The distinction is consequential for measurement. An endpoint-substituted lag can display a nonzero width contrast with no seed variation even when its generalization event is never observed. Reporting event attainment, fitting times, and the observation boundary alongside that statistic is essential to its interpretation. A stronger account of width-dependent delayed generalization would need observed transitions, more initialization and split replication, and controls separating width, initialization scale, and regularization. Those measurements are not supplied here. The present evidence instead establishes which part of the scale question can be answered within the measured budget, and which part remains unidentified.\n+An endpoint-substituted lag can show a nonzero width contrast without seed variation despite entirely unobserved generalization. It must be interpreted alongside event attainment, fitting times, and the observation boundary. Identifying an eventual width-dependent transition requires observed generalization, additional seed and split replication, and controls separating width, initialization scale, and regularization. These unavailable measurements delimit the present finite-horizon evidence.\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\npython3 .codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_compile_inputs.py run -- pdflatex -recorder -no-shell-escape -interaction=nonstopmode -halt-on-error paper.tex > /tmp/paper-repair-pdflatex-4.log 2>&1\npython3 .codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_compile_inputs.py run -- pdflatex -recorder -no-shell-escape -interaction=nonstopmode -halt-on-error paper.tex > /tmp/paper-repair-pdflatex-5.log 2>&1\ntail -3 /tmp/paper-repair-pdflatex-5.log\n/tmp/paper-repair-tools/bin/python - <<'PY'\nimport importlib.util\nimport pymupdf\npaper=pymupdf.open('paper.pdf')\npage_texts=[]\nfor page in paper:\n lines=[]\n for block in page.get_text('dict')['blocks']:\n  if block['type']==0:\n   for line in block['lines']:\n    if line['dir']==(1.,0.) and line['bbox'][0]>100:\n     lines.append(''.join(span['text'] for span in line['spans']))\n page_texts.append('\\\\n'.join(lines))\nprint('Total pages:',len(paper))\nfor index,text in enumerate(page_texts,1):\n if 'REFERENCES' in text or 'SUPPLEMENTARY INFORMATION' in text:\n  print('Section:',index,text[:55])\nspec=importlib.util.spec_from_file_location('validate_rendered_si','.codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_rendered_si.py')\nvalidator=importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)\nspec.loader.exec_module(validator)\nerrors=validator.validate_rendered_supplementary_information(page_texts)\nprint('Canonical SI function, horizontal-body-text extraction:',errors)\nassert not errors\npaper[7].get_pixmap(matrix=pymupdf.Matrix(1,1)).save('/tmp/paper-repair-body-eight.png')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
